# Styling — Tailwind v4

Tailwind v4 (config-less, theme in `src/index.css`) + `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`
for conditional/merged classes. `class-variance-authority` for component variants.

## 1. No Arbitrary Values — the Hard Rule
Do **not** ship bracketed / arbitrary Tailwind values. If you're typing `[` in a
class, stop.

| ❌ Never | ✅ Instead |
|---|---|
| `bg-[#F5F5F5]`, `text-[#1F9D8A]` | a semantic token (`bg-muted`) or a new CSS var (§3) |
| `p-[15px]`, `gap-[7px]` | nearest scale step — `p-4` (16px) / `p-3.5` (14px), `gap-2` |
| `text-[13px]` | `text-sm` / `text-xs` |
| `w-[342px]`, `h-[200px]` | `w-full` + `max-w-sm`, flex/grid sizing, or a scale value |
| `top-[7px]`, `-mt-[3px]` | `top-2`, `-mt-0.5` |
| `rounded-[10px]` | `rounded-lg` (radius scale is defined in `@theme`) |

- Round to the **nearest** Tailwind step; don't invent pixel-perfect values.
- Spacing scale reminder: `1`=4px, `1.5`=6px, `2`=8px, `3`=12px, `3.5`=14px,
  `4`=16px, `5`=20px, `6`=24px, `8`=32px, `10`=40px, `12`=48px.

## 2. Colors
Order of preference:
1. **Semantic tokens** from `@theme inline` in `src/index.css` — always first
   choice because they theme (light/dark) and match the design system:
   `bg-background` `text-foreground` `bg-card` `text-card-foreground`
   `bg-popover` `bg-primary` `text-primary-foreground` `bg-secondary`
   `bg-muted` `text-muted-foreground` `bg-accent` `bg-destructive`
   `border-border` `border-input` `ring-ring` `bg-sidebar` `bg-sidebar-accent`
   `bg-chart-1`…`bg-chart-5`.
2. **Standard Tailwind color classes** (`text-red-600`, `bg-emerald-50`) only for
   incidental, non-branded needs where no token fits (e.g. a one-off callout).
   Still no hex.
3. **A new CSS variable** (§3) if it's a real design color used more than once.

- Never a raw hex/rgb/oklch in a class or `style` prop for a static color.
- Charts get colors from `ChartConfig` referencing `--chart-*` vars — never
  hardcoded series colors.

## 3. Adding a Color
If a needed color isn't a token and isn't a Tailwind palette class, define it
in `src/index.css` — **all three** places:

```css
/* :root */
--brand: oklch(0.63 0.11 183);
--brand-foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);

/* .dark  (pick the dark-mode value) */
--brand: oklch(0.7 0.1 183);
--brand-foreground: oklch(0.205 0 0);

/* @theme inline */
--color-brand: var(--brand);
--color-brand-foreground: var(--brand-foreground);
```

Then use `bg-brand` / `text-brand-foreground`. Name by role (`--brand`,
`--success`, `--warning`), not by hue (`--teal`).

## 4. Legitimate Dynamic Values
Runtime-computed dimensions (a chart height from props, a progress width from a
percentage) are **not** arbitrary Tailwind — pass them via `style` or a CSS
custom property:

```tsx
<div style={{ height: chartHeight }} />
<div className="w-[--w]" style={{ '--w': `${percent}%` } as React.CSSProperties} />
```

Keep this to genuinely dynamic cases; static layout stays in utility classes.

## 5. General
- Compose primitives; don't fight `components/ui/*` internals with overrides.
  Pass `className` for spacing/layout, use the component's `variant`/`size` props
  for the rest.
- RTL + responsive rules live in @rtl.md — logical utilities only
  (`ps/pe`, `ms/me`, `start/end`, `text-start/end`, `border-s/e`), mobile-first,
  works in `ar` + `en`. Never `pl/pr`, `ml/mr`, `left/right`, `text-left/right`.
- Reach for `@apply` in `src/index.css` only for true base-layer element
  defaults, not to bundle component styles.
